---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const internal = (segment) => `${base}/${segment.replace(/^\//, '')}`;
---
<Layout
  title="Definition"
  description="The canonical definition of Agalmic Research: expanding the capacity to discover, choose and realize worthwhile futures while understanding and displacing binding constraints."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Canonical programme definition · v0.2</p>
      <h1>What Agalmic Research is for.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Agalmic Research studies how knowledge, technology and institutions can expand the set of worthwhile futures people can actually reach.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell thesis">
      <p class="eyebrow">Canonical definition</p>
      <blockquote>Agalmic Research studies how knowledge, technology and institutions can expand the set of worthwhile futures people can actually reach.</blockquote>
      <p>It asks which constraints on worthwhile human capability can be made less binding, which new bottlenecks emerge when they are relaxed, and how those bottlenecks can themselves be understood and displaced.</p>
      <p>It treats progress as a continuing process of search, selection and realization rather than as an automatic consequence of technological advance, artificial intelligence or economic growth. Abundance in one dimension may create scarcity in another, including attention, judgment, verification, coordination, resources or the capacity to act.</p>
      <p>Its aim is not abundance for its own sake, nor the production of ever more knowledge or capability, but increasing the capacity to discover, choose and realize worthwhile futures while minimizing harm and avoidable externalities.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What changed</p>
        <h2>Constraint relaxation is the mechanism, not the destination.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">The earlier definition remains accurate, but it no longer carries the whole programme.</p>
        <p>Agalmic Research still asks which constraints can be made less binding and which new bottlenecks appear when they are. That formulation now sits inside a broader purpose: expand the capacity to reach worthwhile futures.</p>
        <div class="callout"><p><strong>Making something abundant can expose a new scarcity. Producing more possibilities can expose a scarcity of selection. Increasing capability can also increase harm. Direction therefore matters.</strong></p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Research discipline</p>
        <h2>A direction is not a result.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>The definition states what the programme is trying to increase and what it refuses to assume. It does not establish that a particular technology, institution or intervention is agalmic.</p>
        <p>Claims still need lineage, explicit assumptions, methods, evidence or argument, criticism and an honest epistemic status. Terms such as <em>worthwhile</em>, <em>broadly useful</em>, <em>harm</em> and <em>avoidable externality</em> also contain normative questions that technical optimization cannot settle by itself.</p>
        <p><a href={internal('research')}>Explore the research programme →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell thesis">
      <p class="eyebrow">Compact form</p>
      <blockquote>The goal is not more ideas. It is greater capacity to reach worthwhile futures.</blockquote>
      <p>The compact form states the direction. The canonical definition explains the search, selection, realization and constraint-displacement machinery beneath it.</p>
      <p><a href={internal('manifesto')}>Read the Agalmic Manifesto →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
